-- title:
--   Ramification function of a quotient: i_{G/H}(τ̄) via sum_{h∈ H} i_G(τ h)
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, with its normalised additive valuation `IsDiscreteValuationRing.addVal R : R → ℕ∞`, and let $G$ be a group acting on $R$ by ring automorphisms, the action being faithful. Let $A$ be a commutative semiring equipped with an algebra structure on $R$, and assume that every $\sigma \in G$ fixes every element $\mathrm{algebraMap}_{A\to R}(a)$, $a \in A$. Let $H$ be a finite normal subgroup of $G$, so that the quotient $G/H$ acts on the subring `FixedPoints.subring R H` of $H$-invariant elements of $R$. Assume there is $x \in R$ with $A[x] = R$ (the $A$-subalgebra generated by $\{x\}$ is $\top$), and an element $y$ of the fixed subring such that every $z$ in the fixed subring lies in the $A$-subalgebra generated by $\{y\}$. Then for every $\tau \in G$, writing $\bar\tau$ for its image in $G/H$,
--   $$\inf_{z \in R^{H}} \mathrm{addVal}_R(\bar\tau \cdot z - z) \;=\; \sum_{h \in H} \Big(\inf_{w \in R} \mathrm{addVal}_R((\tau h) \cdot w - w)\Big),$$
--   the infima being taken in $\mathbb{N} \cup \{\infty\}$ and the differences on the left computed in $R$ after inclusion of the fixed subring; the inner infimum on the right is [`IsDiscreteValuationRing.ramificationDepth R G (τ * h)`](def/Mathlib_RingTheory_Valuation_LowerRamificationGroupDepth.html#L93).
--
--   This is Serre's formula comparing the ramification function of a quotient group with that of the full group, in the form: the infimum of $v_R(\bar\tau z - z)$ over the $H$-fixed subring equals $\sum_{h \in H} i_G(\tau h)$, under monogenicity of $R$ and of $R^H$ over $A$; dividing the left-hand side by the ramification index of $R$ over $R^H$ recovers the classical statement $i_{G/H}(\bar\tau) = e^{-1}\sum_{s \mapsto \bar\tau} i_G(s)$. It is used to show that lower ramification subgroups of $G$ map onto the corresponding lower ramification subgroups of $G/H$, via [`IsDiscreteValuationRing.map_lowerRamificationGroup_mk_eq_of_adjoin_singleton_eq_top`](thm.html#IsDiscreteValuationRing.map_lowerRamificationGroup_mk_eq_of_adjoin_singleton_eq_top).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsDiscreteValuationRing_iInf_addVal_smul_sub_eq_sum_ramificationDepth_of_adjoin_singleton_eq_top.lean

